{"type":"match","data":{"path":{"text":"rocketexpansion.com/20 Best Book Awards Of 2025.txt"},"lines":{"text":"A counterpart to the Booker Prize, the International Booker Prize was established in 2005. Originally presented biennially, in 2016 it had become an annual occurrence. Awarded to a single book published in Ireland or the United Kingdom, the work has to have been published in or translated into English. The prize is shared and split between the author and the translator of the winning book.\n"},"line_number":48,"absolute_offset":1736,"submatches":[{"match":{"text":"International Booker Prize"},"start":39,"end":65}]}}
{"type":"match","data":{"path":{"text":"rocketexpansion.com/20 Best Book Awards Of 2025.txt"},"lines":{"text":"Of all these book awards, the most prestigious are the Nobel Prize in Literature, the Pulitzer Prize, the Booker Prize, the International Booker Prize, PEN America Literary Awards, and the National Book Award.\n"},"line_number":106,"absolute_offset":3995,"submatches":[{"match":{"text":"International Booker Prize"},"start":124,"end":150}]}}
